{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["And the sense of <b>and his hands were emunah</b> is that they remained standing and firm in their elevation, as in the language of \"and a firm ordering for the rulers, a daily matter\" (Nehemiah 11:23), and likewise \"we are cutting a firm covenant\" (ibid. 10:11) — a matter established firmly in a covenant, and similarly \"the peg fastened in a firm place\" (Isaiah 22:23) — strong. And by way of truth, he raised ten fingers toward the height of heaven to allude to the ten sefirot, to cleave to the emunah that does battle for Israel, and from this the matter of the raising of hands in the priestly blessing is explained, and its secret."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:09:47.625910320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}